WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.434
Hi! Where does your lunch go after you eat it? Today we'll meet the body's systems, then follow food through the digestive system.

2
00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:16.794
The digestive system breaks down food into simpler substances that the body can absorb.

3
00:00:16.944 --> 00:00:23.538
The respiratory system, with the nose and lungs, takes in oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide.

4
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:32.058
The circulatory system, the heart and blood vessels, carries digested food, water and oxygen around the body.

5
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:41.394
The skeleton supports the body and protects organs; the ribs protect the heart and lungs. Muscles pull on bones so we can move.

6
00:00:41.544 --> 00:00:56.298
These systems work together. Digested food absorbed in the small intestine needs the circulatory system to carry it to every part of the body. And when you lift your arm, your muscles contract and pull on your bones.

7
00:00:56.448 --> 00:01:02.658
The digestive system is like a long tube. Food passes through five parts in order.

8
00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:10.890
First, the mouth. Teeth chew the food into small pieces, and saliva, a digestive juice, starts digestion.

9
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:17.778
Next, the gullet. It only moves food down to the stomach. No digestion happens here.

10
00:01:17.928 --> 00:01:24.810
Then the stomach. It churns the food and mixes it with digestive juices, and digestion continues.

11
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:34.242
Next, the small intestine. Digestion is completed here, and digested food is absorbed into the blood, which carries it round the body.

12
00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:45.042
Last, the large intestine. It absorbs water, and no digestion happens. Undigested food leaves the body through the anus.

13
00:01:45.192 --> 00:01:50.154
Watch out! Not every part that food passes through digests it!

14
00:01:50.304 --> 00:01:59.298
There is no digestion in the gullet or the large intestine. The gullet only moves food, and the large intestine only absorbs water.

15
00:01:59.448 --> 00:02:06.930
Digestion starts in the mouth, continues in the stomach and is completed in the small intestine.

16
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:16.482
Your turn! In which part is digested food absorbed into the blood? Pause and think.

17
00:02:16.632 --> 00:02:29.682
The small intestine. Digestion is completed there, and digested food passes into the blood. The large intestine takes in water, not digested food. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:38.874
Another one! Why should we chew our food well before swallowing? Pause and think.

19
00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:49.410
Chewing breaks food into smaller pieces, so digestive juices can act on it more easily and it is digested faster. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:59.178
Last one! Put these five parts in the order that food passes through them. Pause and think.

21
00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:07.674
Mouth, gullet, stomach, small intestine, large intestine. Did you get it right?

22
00:03:07.824 --> 00:03:14.874
Remember: the digestive system breaks down food into simple substances the body can absorb.

23
00:03:15.024 --> 00:03:26.874
The mouth starts digestion, the gullet moves food, the stomach continues, the small intestine completes digestion and absorbs food, and the large intestine absorbs water.

24
00:03:27.024 --> 00:03:31.338
At your next meal, remember to chew well!

